{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unclean-crazed-gavial","creation_channel":"python","description":"# J8 — ADR amending 0035: the Jira-family sub-seam, shared provenance, and the DC horizon\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nADR 0035 §6 states that \"the first real second backend is out of scope for this ADR and is tracked separately\nby epic `be74-7832-03a8-48ac`\" — the GitHub adapter. This epic lands a different second backend first, and it\nintroduces a structure ADR 0035 does not describe: a `jira_family` layer between the neutral core and a\nconcrete adapter, with two contracts (`RichTextCodec`, `UserIdentityModel`) parameterizing it. It also makes a\nprovenance decision — that the Jira family shares one `jira` creation channel and `jira-` id prefix, with\ndeployments distinguished by `RemoteRef.instance` — which is precisely the decision PR #120 would have made\nsilently by inheriting the hardcoded literal at `apply_inbound_records.py:163`. And it adds rebar's first\nthird-party runtime dependency in the reconciler, confined to an extra.\n\nLeft unrecorded, each of these gets re-litigated the next time a Jira-like tracker appears.\n\n## Approach\n\nWrite one ADR that amends 0035 rather than replacing it, recording: the `adapters/jira_family/` layer and why\nthe seam is now two levels for one vendor family; the two parameterizing contracts; the shared-`jira`\nprovenance decision and explicitly what it defers to epic `be74` (generalizing `jira_key`, the `jira-` prefix,\nand the channel vocabulary when a genuinely different vendor lands); the `pycontribs/jira` dependency, why it is\nextra-gated, and why the Cloud ACLI path was deliberately not migrated onto it; and the Docker harness as the\nverification oracle given that DC trial licenses ended in March 2026 and no official DC OpenAPI spec exists.\n\nThe ADR states the **horizon** plainly: Data Center goes read-only on 28 March 2029 and receives no new\nfeatures today, so this is a deliberately time-boxed investment for existing self-hosted clients, and the\ndurable asset is the family seam rather than the DC adapter. That framing is what tells a future maintainer\nwhether to extend this code or retire it.\n\n**Alternative rejected:** documenting only in `docs/architecture.md`. rebar's ADR set is where rejected\nalternatives live; without them the fork-per-deployment and hand-rolled-client options get re-proposed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `docs/adr/00NN-jira-family-sub-seam.md` (new).\n- `docs/adr/0035-reconciler-vendor-adapter-seam.md` — a pointer noting the amendment and correcting §6's\n  \"first real second backend\" statement.\n- `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/user-guide.md` — the `reconciler.backend` choice and the DC extra.\n- `docs/env-vars.md` — regenerated for `JIRA_PAT`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/user-guide.md` states the DC least-privilege expectation: a dedicated service account whose PAT is\n      scoped to only the reconciled projects (Browse Projects / Create Issues / Edit Issues / Add Comments /\n      Link Issues), never an admin token — and documents `allow_insecure` as cleartext-only-if-you-must, the\n      `ca_bundle` key for internal-CA certificates, and `resolved_statuses` for workflows that do not use the\n      conventional Resolved/Done/Cancelled state names (epic AC13)\n- [ ] the ADR exists, is `Accepted`, and records each rejected alternative (fork-per-deployment, hand-rolled\n      stdlib client, generalizing the store vocabulary now, migrating Cloud onto pycontribs) with its reason\n- [ ] ADR 0035 carries a pointer to the amendment and its §6 statement is corrected\n- [ ] the ADR states the March 2029 DC read-only date and what it implies for future investment in this adapter\n- [ ] `docs/user-guide.md` documents selecting the DC backend and installing the extra, and the documented\n      commands have been executed against the J5 harness\n- [ ] `docs/env-vars.md` regenerates with no diff","id":"ca24-5f77-1d4c-4bce","parent_id":"cbca-7684-3df1-4a01","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"J8 — ADR amending 0035: the Jira-family sub-seam, shared provenance, and the DC horizon"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788224325869485001,"uuid":"9488cd17-b198-4e91-ba5d-d3634b59af38"}